342
00:22:12,060 --> 00:22:13,680
So how long is a biblical fast?

343
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:20,540
Besides the one that's commanded in the day of atonement, 24 hours, there's no set rules, just examples.

344
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:22,420
So this is between you and God.

345
00:22:22,420 --> 00:22:27,100
Most common fasts are sun up to sun down or 24 hours.

346
00:22:27,780 --> 00:22:37,640
There are some examples of three-day fasts, seven-day fasts, 21-day fasts, and again, very rare examples of 40-day fasts, most of which are supernaturally empowered.

347
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:43,040
So the key here is it's up to you and your community and God.

348
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:47,120
Seek the Lord and ask him what he might be inviting you into.

349
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:52,580
All of this is an invitation for you to pursue God with your whole selves, which we'll get to when we get to the theology part.

350
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,780
This is an invitation.

351
00:22:54,780 --> 00:23:00,960
This is not a legalistic requirement that you have to do in order to be called a mature Christian.

352
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:02,820
This is an invitation.

353
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:06,320
I love what Arthur Willis says.

354
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:06,680
He says,

355
00:23:06,680 --> 00:23:20,420
When we fast, how long we fast, the nature of the fast, and the spiritual objectives of the fast are all God's choice, to which the obedient disciple gladly responds.

356
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:23,240
I'd add one last caveat here.

357
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:32,420
If you feel the Lord calling you to fast longer than 24 hours, don't do it without reading a couple of books, doing some research, and talking to your doctor.

358
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:37,280
There's best practices for these things, and it would be foolish of you to just say,

359
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:39,040
Oh, the Lord told me to fast for seven days.

360
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:39,880
I'm just going to do it.

361
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:42,580
There's wisdom here, all right?

362
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:47,240
Were any of you feeling like you were just going to fast for seven days and not reading any books?

363
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:47,920
I didn't think so.

364
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:50,700
But I had to add that there for my own edification.

365
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,800
When should we fast?

366
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,100
Again, up to you.

367
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:55,500
Prayerfully seek the Lord.

368
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:59,800
Scripture and history gives us two specific examples.

369
00:24:00,580 --> 00:24:03,760
One is a regular rhythm throughout history in the church.

370
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:10,780
Certain seasons or times, there would be regular rhythms of fasting, weekly, monthly, or during specific seasons of the year.

371
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:13,780
And then secondly, an intentional response.

372
00:24:13,780 --> 00:24:22,320
A lot of the fasts we see in the Old Testament are individuals or communities responding to grief, lament, repenting from sin,

373
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:29,880
or entering a season of specific prayer where they're asking God to show up and do something that seems supernatural and impossible.

374
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:33,240
So, regular rhythm and intentional response.

375
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:36,140
Again, this is all up to you.

376
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:37,540
Sound good?

377
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:39,160
All right.

