00:29:44,360 --> 00:29:48,520
Or who has given a gift to him that he might be repaid?

466
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:55,120
For from him, and through him, and to him are all things.

467
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:57,460
To him be the glory forever.

468
00:29:57,460 --> 00:29:58,840
Amen.

469
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:02,300
I appeal to you, therefore, brothers,

470
00:30:02,300 --> 00:30:07,820
by the mercies of God to present your bodies as a living sacrifice,

471
00:30:07,820 --> 00:30:09,940
holy and acceptable to God,

472
00:30:09,940 --> 00:30:12,680
which is your spiritual worship.

473
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:15,320
Do not be conformed to this world,

474
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:18,000
but be transformed by the renewal of your mind,

475
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:21,360
that by testing you may discern what is the will of God,

476
00:30:21,360 --> 00:30:24,680
what is good and acceptable and perfect.

477
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:26,640
This is the word of the Lord.

478
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:27,880
Thank you.

479
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,120
Thank you.

480
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:29,860
You guys can be seated.

481
00:30:29,860 --> 00:30:35,480
So, this passage, I know I say this a lot.

482
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:38,120
One of my favorite passages in all of Scripture.

483
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:43,620
This is actually the passage that was used by the camp speaker

484
00:30:43,620 --> 00:30:49,000
that led me, ultimately, to give my life and allegiance to Jesus.

485
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:53,400
And I love this passage because at the end of Romans chapter 11,

486
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:59,960
what Paul has done is Paul has laid out as clearly and as detailed as he ever has

487
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:02,560
his explanation of what the gospel is,

488
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:08,700
of the implications of Jesus dying, burying, and being raised to new life for our salvation.

489
00:31:09,780 --> 00:31:14,360
It's a detailed explanation of the gospel to people that he's never met before.

490
00:31:14,360 --> 00:31:18,000
So, he goes in as much detail as he possibly can.

491
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:22,340
Chapters 1 through 11 are incredibly profound.

492
00:31:22,340 --> 00:31:26,100
And then at chapter 12, he makes a shift and he says,

493
00:31:26,100 --> 00:31:29,640
because of all of these things, in light of all of these mercies,

494
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,400
because all of these things are true,

495
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:35,140
this is how you should live your life in response to the gospel of Jesus.

496
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:41,060
It's this hinge passage where he takes theology and leads to practice.

497
00:31:41,060 --> 00:31:46,640
He takes information about God and invites you into obedience to God.

498
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:49,700
And I love that he literally can't help himself.

499
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:54,520
He finishes his most detailed explanation of the gospel

500
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:58,080
and like spilling out of him is a hymn of praise.

501
00:31:58,080 --> 00:32:01,220
That's what chapter 11, verse 33 through 36 is.

502
00:32:01,220 --> 00:32:03,840
It's literally Paul's response to the gospel.

503
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:08,120
Oh, how deep are the riches and the wisdom and the knowledge of God.

504
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:10,300
How unsearchable are his judgments.

505
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:11,840
Who has known the mind of God?

506
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:15,920
From him and through him and to him are all things.

507
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:19,940
This is Paul's response to the good news of Jesus.

508
00:32:19,940 --> 00:32:21,380
It's a hymn of praise.

509
00:32:21,380 --> 00:32:23,420
And then he says,

510
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:25,760
Because all of this is true.

511
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:30,200
By the mercies of God, present your what?

512
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:34,480
Present your bodies.

513
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:38,100
A living sacrifice, holy and acceptable to God,

514
00:32:38,100 --> 00:32:39,760
which is your what kind of worship?

515
00:32:39,760 --> 00:32:43,040
Spiritual worship.

516
00:32:43,040 --> 00:32:48,420
So somehow, presenting our bodies becomes a spiritual worship.

517
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:50,100
Physical bodies, spiritual worship.

518
00:32:50,100 --> 00:32:51,380
There seems to be a connection there, right?

519
00:32:52,880 --> 00:32:56,060
Okay, so Paul says,

520
00:32:56,060 --> 00:32:59,780
This is not a blind response to a distant dictator in the sky,

521
00:32:59,780 --> 00:33:05,160
but presenting your bodies to God is a loving response to a God

522
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:07,540
who loves you and has offered himself to you.

523
00:33:07,540 --> 00:33:08,580
This is what he means when he says,

524
00:33:08,580 --> 00:33:12,920
In view of God's mercy, because of what God has done for you,

525
00:33:12,920 --> 00:33:15,660
you now offer your entire selves to God.

526
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:18,440
Here's my main point for our time this morning.

527
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:24,460
My main point is this, that fasting is a practice aimed at offering our entire selves to God

528
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:27,980
so that he can transform us into the image of Jesus.

529
00:33:27,980 --> 00:33:32,100
It should be on the screen, but I will say it one more time, yes.

530
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:36,980
Fasting is a, emphasis on a, not the only practice.

531
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:41,980
Fasting is a practice aimed at offering our entire selves to God

532
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:46,160
so that he can transform us into the image of Jesus.

533
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:52,560
This passage is at the heart of why I feel so strongly about this entire series,

534
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:55,400
not just these four weeks, but all of the nine practices.

535
00:33:55,400 --> 00:34:00,940
Because most of the spiritual practices we regularly discuss in the West

536
00:34:00,940 --> 00:34:02,740
are aimed at our mind or our hearts.

537
00:34:02,740 --> 00:34:08,020
Bible reading, worship, prayer, these tend to be in our minds and in our hearts.

538
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:16,100
And I'm trying to ask us to diversify ways in which we might consider to offer our entire selves to God.

539
00:34:16,100 --> 00:34:22,740
Not only that, fasting is one of the three main practices that Jesus addresses in his most prominent sermon.

540
00:34:22,740 --> 00:34:29,340
He addresses in the Sermon on the Mount, giving to the poor, fasting, and praying.

541
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:31,900
Bible reading?

542
00:34:34,160 --> 00:34:38,300
Okay, take the, I'm going to get some emails, good grief.

543
00:34:38,300 --> 00:34:40,780
That was not in my notes, I'm sorry, don't hold that against me.

544
00:34:40,780 --> 00:34:47,320
Alright, so part of the reason I think many of us in the West naturally react against fasting

545
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:53,240
is because we've been subversively discipled by two ideologies that have creeped into the church

546
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:55,600
and have shaped the way that we think about our bodies.

547
00:34:55,600 --> 00:34:59,600
I've talked about this before, but you're going to get a flyover really quick.

548
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:01,120
The first is called hedonism.

549
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:07,780
Hedonism is an influence of our culture that essentially says your physical comfort and your pleasure

550
00:35:07,780 --> 00:35:09,580
is the chief end of man.

551
00:35:09,580 --> 00:35:11,720
We see this in our culture.

552
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:14,900
Just pursue your satisfaction.

553
00:35:14,900 --> 00:35:19,420
Whatever makes you feel good, you do it and you keep doing it

554
00:35:19,420 --> 00:35:22,740
and you don't let anybody tell you what you can or cannot do with your body.

555
00:35:23,160 --> 00:35:26,360
Avoid anything that makes you uncomfortable at all costs.

556
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:29,700
Surround yourself with people who agree with your ideology

557
00:35:29,700 --> 00:35:33,980
and who will approve of you doing whatever it is that makes you happy and satisfied.

558
00:35:33,980 --> 00:35:36,140
Do we see this?

559
00:35:36,140 --> 00:35:40,540
Here's the problem with this ideology.

560
00:35:40,540 --> 00:35:41,900
Many problems.

561
00:35:41,900 --> 00:35:47,220
One of the biggest problems with this ideology is that our world is broken by sin.

562
00:35:48,160 --> 00:35:54,200
And no matter how hard you try to find ultimate satisfaction and physical pleasure,

563
00:35:54,200 --> 00:35:56,320
something in your life will happen.

564
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:58,600
Your body will get sick.

565
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,640
A friend or a loved one will die.

566
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:02,580
A relationship will be broken.

567
00:36:02,580 --> 00:36:04,600
Bad things will happen.

568
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:08,720
And if you don't have a theology for suffering, you're setting yourself up for failure.

569
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:12,780
So hedonism has creeped into the church.

570
00:36:12,780 --> 00:36:17,020
And we talk about, I talk about the abundant life all the time, right?

571
00:36:17,020 --> 00:36:21,940
But we overemphasize sometimes too much the physical pleasures of this world.

572
00:36:21,940 --> 00:36:26,120
And we say, well, if we just obey Jesus, then our physical lives will be great.

573
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,720
And we ignore the spiritual realm.

574
00:36:27,720 --> 00:36:30,580
The opposite side of the coin is also true.

575
00:36:30,580 --> 00:36:34,300
There's Gnostic and Platonistic influences in the church.

576
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:41,800
This message says that the gospel is primarily about saving your souls from eternal judgment.

577
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:45,500
That our bodies in this world are of little spiritual value.

578
00:36:45,500 --> 00:36:50,500
No self-respecting Christian says that your body doesn't matter at all.

579
00:36:50,500 --> 00:36:53,560
But it's creeping into our thoughts and our lives.

580
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:56,900
And we say, well, what really matters is what you do spiritually.

581
00:36:56,900 --> 00:36:59,540
And what you do in the body, like, it kind of matters, right?

582
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:09,860
The Christian cliche for both of these ideologies is we say people are so heavenly focused that they're no, we've heard that, right?

583
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:14,080
Or that they're so earthly focused that they're no heavenly good.

584
00:37:14,080 --> 00:37:18,680
And the problem is that both of these ideologies are a distortion of the gospel.

585
00:37:19,720 --> 00:37:29,980
The first line of the Bible is God created the heavens and the, God created the physical and the spiritual.

586
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:33,180
Jesus came to earth in a physical body.

587
00:37:33,180 --> 00:37:36,780
He was raised from the dead in a physical body.

588
00:37:36,780 --> 00:37:42,280
New Testament theology of salvation includes us receiving resurrected bodies.

589
00:37:42,280 --> 00:37:47,320
And the meta-narrative of the Bible is about God bringing heaven to earth.

590
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:49,680
This is the temple of the Old Testament.

591
00:37:49,680 --> 00:37:52,280
They built the temple and God's presence dwelt.

592
00:37:52,280 --> 00:37:53,800
He brought heaven to earth.

593
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:56,940
That was a shadow of what he was ultimately going to do in Jesus.

594
00:37:56,940 --> 00:38:00,080
We read in Revelation that ultimately the heaven will come to earth.

595
00:38:00,080 --> 00:38:02,260
This is what we learn to pray in the Lord's Prayer.

596
00:38:02,260 --> 00:38:03,860
Lord, your kingdom come.

597
00:38:03,860 --> 00:38:07,860
Your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

598
00:38:07,860 --> 00:38:12,900
There's this connection between the spiritual and the physical.

599
00:38:12,900 --> 00:38:18,140
And if we lose sight of it, we tend to overemphasize one or the other.

600
00:38:18,140 --> 00:38:22,780
And fasting in some mysterious way blends the two.

601
00:38:22,780 --> 00:38:29,240
It reminds us that our bodies are not just things carrying around our souls.

602
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:31,080
That our bodies matter to God.

603
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:36,880
That what we do in the physical world has implications for the spiritual world.

604
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:39,200
1 Corinthians 6, Paul doubles down on this.

605
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:39,520
He says,

606
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:47,480
Do you not know your bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received from God?

607
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:48,900
You are not your own.

608
00:38:48,900 --> 00:38:50,840
You were bought with a price.

609
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:56,260
Therefore, honor God with your bodies.

610
00:38:57,460 --> 00:39:05,500
There's such deep application in this passage in understanding that your bodies become a new place where heaven and earth dwell together.

611
00:39:05,500 --> 00:39:08,700
The physical and the spiritual both exist at the same time.

612
00:39:08,700 --> 00:39:16,080
The death, burial, and resurrection of Jesus doesn't just offer you a hope in the mysterious future after death.

613
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:21,480
But it has incredible hope and redemption and resurrection power for your life today.

614
00:39:21,480 --> 00:39:25,600
Abundant life now and eternal life in the future.

615
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:28,340
We've got to learn to hold both of these together.

616
00:39:28,340 --> 00:39:36,680
Now, many of us in this room have very negative views of ourselves.

617
00:39:36,680 --> 00:39:38,600
Of our physical bodies.

618
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:42,720
We have deep trauma that we carry in our bodies.

619
00:39:42,720 --> 00:39:46,360
Because of cultural beauty standards.

620
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:49,520
Because of sin that we've committed in the past.

621
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:53,480
Or because of things that have happened to us that are outside of our control.

622
00:39:56,600 --> 00:40:04,600
The gospel of Jesus has the power to bring redemption and hope for your self-image.

623
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:09,600
The good news of the message of Jesus is that God loves you.

624
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:11,040
He loves all of you.

625
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:13,220
He created you on purpose.

626
00:40:13,220 --> 00:40:15,280
He knit you together in your mother's womb.

627
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:17,320
You are fearfully and wonderfully made.

628
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:24,380
There is nothing that you could do or that could be done to you that could lessen your value before the God who made you and loves you.

629
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:33,080
We lose so much of the culture of this passage because the temple, the temple was like the shining light of the Jewish people.

630
00:40:33,080 --> 00:40:35,000
It was the best thing that they had.

631
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,020
It was the most beautiful thing that they've had.

632
00:40:37,020 --> 00:40:41,000
And Paul says, your bodies are that to God.

633
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:45,160
Your bodies matter to God.

634
00:40:45,160 --> 00:40:47,020
What we do with them matters to God.

635
00:40:47,020 --> 00:40:51,560
And so fasting is this offering of ourselves to God.

636
00:40:51,560 --> 00:40:54,820
Our physical selves to God in a spiritual way.

637
00:40:54,820 --> 00:40:58,220
It's a physical action that has spiritual implications.

638
00:40:58,220 --> 00:41:00,480
Scott McKnight calls it body talk.

639
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:04,520
It's a way of praying with our entire selves.

640
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:14,020
It's a way of putting to practice this passage in Romans chapter 12 of offering our bodies, our whole selves to God as a living sacrifice.

641
00:41:14,960 --> 00:41:19,100
It's mysterious in a way, and I'd be lying to you if I said I fully understood it.

642
00:41:19,100 --> 00:41:21,140
But here's what I'll tell you.

643
00:41:21,140 --> 00:41:27,540
The God who created our bodies and our souls invites us to practice this.

644
00:41:27,540 --> 00:41:34,100
Jesus who created you, who came to the earth to live a perfect life in your place, to die for your sins.

645
00:41:34,100 --> 00:41:37,100
He says, when you fast.

646
00:41:38,700 --> 00:41:43,920
What if we just trusted him and received this invitation?

647
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:48,800
What if we just tried something that was outside of our comfort zones?

648
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:59,160
What if we just saw that he might show up in supernatural ways like many of us who have followed him for any time at all know that oftentimes he shows up in ways that are so beyond our understanding?

649
00:41:59,160 --> 00:42:05,160
Oh, the depth of the riches and wisdom and knowledge of God.

650
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:08,000
His ways are higher than our ways.

651
00:42:08,540 --> 00:42:10,280
His thoughts are higher than our thoughts.

652
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:13,120
I love what John Piper says.

653
00:42:13,120 --> 00:42:19,660
It says, Christian fasting at its root is the hunger of a homesickness for God.

654
00:42:19,660 --> 00:42:23,220
It's a way of us telling our bodies.

655
00:42:23,220 --> 00:42:32,520
It's a way of us pre-deciding that we are going to hunger for God no matter what the circumstances of our life show us.

656
00:42:33,440 --> 00:42:34,180
I was out.

657
00:42:34,180 --> 00:42:41,240
I don't know why I'm hesitating telling this story.

658
00:42:41,240 --> 00:42:42,940
Okay.

659
00:42:42,940 --> 00:42:44,080
So, Friday.

660
00:42:44,080 --> 00:42:47,560
I was fasting because I took my wife out on Valentine's Day.

661
00:42:47,560 --> 00:42:50,380
I skipped my Wednesday fast, so I moved it to Friday.

662
00:42:50,380 --> 00:42:55,680
And then, of course, Donovan, in his love and kindness for me, knew that I was having a rough couple of weeks.

663
00:42:56,100 --> 00:42:57,360
Friday is supposed to be my day off.

664
00:42:57,360 --> 00:42:59,480
And Donovan said, hey, let's go golfing on Friday.

665
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:02,660
And so, I said, that would be wonderful.

666
00:43:03,420 --> 00:43:09,200
So, he decides that because we're going to be in good shape, we're going to walk nine holes at Blue Ridge Shadows.

667
00:43:09,200 --> 00:43:13,000
If you've ever been to Blue Ridge Shadows at all, it's five.

668
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:17,420
Nine holes is five miles up and down hills over and over and over again.

669
00:43:17,420 --> 00:43:18,620
So, I'm like, oh, great.

670
00:43:18,620 --> 00:43:19,520
I'm fasting.

671
00:43:19,520 --> 00:43:22,800
And I'm walking five miles up and down hills.

672
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:23,820
This is going to be awesome.

673
00:43:23,820 --> 00:43:31,400
And then, because I didn't feel the Lord telling me to tell Donovan I'm fasting, he just kept offering me, like, Reese's Pieces.

674
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:34,620
And, like, he's like, you want a snack?

675
00:43:34,620 --> 00:43:35,140
You want this?

676
00:43:35,140 --> 00:43:35,640
You want that?

677
00:43:35,640 --> 00:43:36,880
I'm like, no, thanks.

678
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:38,620
No, thanks.

679
00:43:38,620 --> 00:43:40,060
No, thanks.

680
00:43:40,060 --> 00:43:45,080
And as I was walking up one of the fairways, and I got this tremendous hunger pain.

681
00:43:46,460 --> 00:43:55,980
And tremendous is really dramatic because I'd, like, less than 24 hours without food, and I'm starving, right?

682
00:43:55,980 --> 00:43:59,340
Again, we'll get to that later, but how dramatic can we be as Americans?

683
00:43:59,340 --> 00:44:10,660
But when I had that hunger pain, and I thought about all of the distractions of my life and all of the things that I was just thinking about, everything but God.

684
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:21,140
And I got this pain in my stomach, and I literally thought to myself, Ryan, you have pre-decided today to hunger for God.

685
00:44:21,140 --> 00:44:29,860
You have made a decision previously that is now bringing your body and your mind, your whole self before the Lord in prayer.

686
00:44:29,860 --> 00:44:31,060
It's body talk.

687
00:44:31,060 --> 00:44:41,420
It reminded me that no matter the circumstances of my day, no matter what comes my way, I've decided that I'm going to hunger for the Lord.

688
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:45,840
And that's my best effort at explaining to you how fasting works.

689
00:44:45,840 --> 00:44:56,340
It's a practice, a practice, aimed at offering your entire self to God so that he could transform you into the image of Jesus.

690
00:44:56,340 --> 00:44:58,740
Look at how Romans chapter 12, verse 2 ends.

691
00:44:58,740 --> 00:44:59,800
What's the point?

692
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:04,040
What's the whole goal of offering ourselves to God as a living sacrifice?

693
00:45:06,200 --> 00:45:06,740
It says,

694
00:45:06,740 --> 00:45:10,700
Do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind.

695
00:45:10,700 --> 00:45:15,260
Again, my intellectual brothers and sisters, I'm not anti-Bible reading and brain.

696
00:45:15,260 --> 00:45:16,560
This is what we're saying here.

697
00:45:16,560 --> 00:45:20,760
That by testing, you may discern what is the will of God.

698
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:25,160
What is good, acceptable, and perfect.

699
00:45:27,320 --> 00:45:33,140
So that seems like kind of supernatural and kind of, hmm, I wonder what the will of God is.

700
00:45:33,140 --> 00:45:33,800
But guess what?

701
00:45:33,800 --> 00:45:38,300
Paul already defined for us what the will of God was in Romans chapter 8.

702
00:45:40,800 --> 00:45:49,560
For those whom he foreknew, he predestined to be conformed to the image of his son in order that we might be the firstborn among many brothers.

703
00:45:49,560 --> 00:45:57,000
We present our whole bodies, our whole selves to God so that God can transform us into a person that looks like Jesus.

704
00:45:57,000 --> 00:46:07,860
Again, if any of these practices are doing anything other than inviting you into a deeper relationship with the God who loves you, who made you, who died to bring you into right relationship with himself, don't do them.

705
00:46:09,700 --> 00:46:18,940
This is the point, that we would pursue Jesus in relationship and that he would transform us into a person of Christ-like love.

706
00:46:18,940 --> 00:46:26,200
So, I realize fasting is brand new to many of us, totally foreign to us in a lot of ways.

707
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:29,720
My prayer is that I didn't create more questions than answers.

708
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:38,880
That being said, I truly believe that this practice is something worth investigating for those of us who are seriously pursuing discipleship to Jesus.

709
00:46:39,080 --> 00:46:40,540
And are physically able.

710
00:46:40,540 --> 00:46:43,800
Again, I'm going to quote Arthur Wallace.

711
00:46:43,800 --> 00:46:44,660
He says this,

712
00:46:44,660 --> 00:46:56,560
In giving us, oh, this is fun, the privilege of fasting, as well as praying, God has added a powerful weapon to our spiritual army.

713
00:46:56,560 --> 00:47:02,140
In her folly and ignorance, the church has largely looked upon it as obsolete.

714
00:47:02,740 --> 00:47:07,220
She has thrown it down in some dark corner to rust, and there it is laying forgotten for centuries.

715
00:47:07,220 --> 00:47:13,180
An hour of impending crisis for the church in the world demands its recovery.

716
00:47:14,680 --> 00:47:26,920
So, if you're a relatively healthy person with no past history of eating disorders, I would prayerfully invite you to consider a sun-up to sun-down fast this week.

717
00:47:26,920 --> 00:47:29,480
One fast less than 24 hours.

718
00:47:29,640 --> 00:47:31,540
Just consider it.

719
00:47:31,540 --> 00:47:33,760
And see what God might do.

720
00:47:33,760 --> 00:47:34,980
How God might show up.

721
00:47:40,980 --> 00:47:43,660
I was listening to a podcast about Lent this past week.

722
00:47:43,660 --> 00:47:51,680
And they said, they were talking about how all of the practices of Lent should be about bringing you into a closer relationship with Jesus.

723
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:57,580
And the illustration they gave, I thought, was so beautiful, and so I want to give it to you as we're kind of concluding.

724
00:47:57,580 --> 00:48:06,500
They said, you know when you're in a room with kids, and the parents are in the room, and you say, like, hey, buddy, do you want to go outside and throw the ball?

725
00:48:06,500 --> 00:48:14,800
And what tends to happen in that moment is both you and the kid look to the parent, and you say, is that all right?

726
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:16,420
Can we go outside?

727
00:48:16,420 --> 00:48:17,060
Can we throw the ball?

728
00:48:17,060 --> 00:48:18,480
Can we do whatever?

729
00:48:18,480 --> 00:48:19,940
You guys ever had that experience?

730
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:35,760
And the illustration that they were saying is, in all of these conversations about Lent and about fasting and about spiritual practices, it's all about you and God, your heavenly Father, who loves you, who made you, who desires you to have a relationship with him.

731
00:48:35,760 --> 00:48:42,440
And so anytime you hear anything from this stage encouraging you to do something, always take it back to God.

732
00:48:42,440 --> 00:48:44,560
Say, God, is this for me?

733
00:48:44,560 --> 00:48:46,660
Are you inviting me into this?

734
00:48:46,660 --> 00:48:48,420
How might you be inviting me into this?

735
00:48:49,760 --> 00:48:56,200
And if there's resistance in your heart towards this practice, if there's a natural reaction against it, pause and consider why.

736
00:48:56,200 --> 00:49:00,400
It's possible you still have more questions because this sermon wasn't any good.

737
00:49:00,400 --> 00:49:08,700
It's possible that you're too consumed with the pleasures that food brings on a day-to-day basis.

738
00:49:10,120 --> 00:49:15,060
It's possible that you are struggling to trust Jesus with your whole self.

739
00:49:15,060 --> 00:49:16,880
No guilt, no shame.

740
00:49:16,880 --> 00:49:18,240
Take this back to God.

741
00:49:18,240 --> 00:49:24,560
In his grace and mercy, he will lead you into life.

742
00:49:26,040 --> 00:49:31,760
If you have health issues or a history of eating disorder, I would just encourage you to consider abstaining from something this week.

743
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:35,080
If you don't know what to abstain from, ask yourself this question.

744
00:49:35,080 --> 00:49:36,920
What is it that consumes me?

745
00:49:36,920 --> 00:49:42,320
Social media, podcasts, TV, YouTube, substances, hobbies.

746
00:49:42,320 --> 00:49:46,600
Give up something that will force you to exercise intentional self-control.

747
00:49:47,600 --> 00:49:50,460
And ask God what he might be revealing to you about yourself in that.

748
00:49:50,460 --> 00:49:55,120
Lastly, if you're not a follower of Jesus, this message was primarily not for you.

749
00:49:55,120 --> 00:49:55,720
I'm sorry.

750
00:49:55,720 --> 00:50:00,740
If you're just curious about the Bible, what I would say is your takeaway for this message.

751
00:50:00,740 --> 00:50:01,520
God loves you.

752
00:50:01,520 --> 00:50:03,360
He loves all of you.

753
00:50:04,360 --> 00:50:16,000
He demonstrated his love for you by sending his son, Jesus, to die in your place for your sins and resurrect it from the dead, giving you the opportunity to experience eternal life in the future and abundant life now.

754
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:23,060
He's inviting you to hand over your life, the leadership of your life to him because he's worthy of it.

755
00:50:26,140 --> 00:50:34,440
If that's something that you're interested in, there's a connect card that you can mark that option or you can come find me after service or find one of our leaders.

756
00:50:34,440 --> 00:50:35,920
We'd love to talk to you about it.

757
00:50:35,920 --> 00:50:40,920
In an effort to be overly clear, one final reminder, there's no pressure or guilt here.

758
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:43,920
This is just an invitation for you to take back to God.

759
00:50:43,920 --> 00:50:50,480
At the end of the day, all of these practices are tools to help you present your entire selves to God.

760
00:50:52,380 --> 00:50:56,840
Love the Lord your God with all of your heart, soul, mind, and strength.

761
00:50:56,840 --> 00:51:05,320
I'm super passionate about this stuff because I believe that the God who created you and loves you is inviting you into deeper intimacy with himself,

762
00:51:05,320 --> 00:51:08,940
which is far better than anything this world has to offer you.

763
00:51:08,940 --> 00:51:15,320
Whatever ways you decide to present yourself to God, I'm believing and trusting that he will show up,

764
00:51:15,320 --> 00:51:22,280
that he will hold up his end of the bargain, and that he will use that surrender to make you into a person of Christ-like love.

765
00:51:22,320 --> 00:51:24,200
We're going to end by reading this passage one more time.

766
00:51:24,200 --> 00:51:33,640
Oh, the depth of the riches and wisdom and knowledge of God.

767
00:51:33,640 --> 00:51:36,000
How unsearchable are his judgments.

768
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:38,280
How inscrutable are his ways.

769
00:51:38,280 --> 00:51:41,820
For who has known the mind of the Lord or who has been his counselor?

770
00:51:41,820 --> 00:51:45,360
Or who has given him a gift that he might be repaid?

771
00:51:45,360 --> 00:51:50,740
For from him and through him and to him are all things.

772
00:51:51,480 --> 00:51:53,680
To him be the glory forever.

773
00:51:53,680 --> 00:52:02,020
Therefore, brothers and sisters, I appeal to you by the mercies of God to present your bodies a living sacrifice,

774
00:52:02,020 --> 00:52:06,320
holy and acceptable to God, which is your spiritual worship.

775
00:52:06,320 --> 00:52:08,940
Don't be conformed to this world.

776
00:52:09,360 --> 00:52:11,900
Be transformed by the renewing of your mind.

777
00:52:11,900 --> 00:52:17,040
That by testing you may discern what is the will of God, what is good, acceptable, and perfect.

778
00:52:17,040 --> 00:52:17,960
Father in heaven,

779
00:52:17,960 --> 00:52:23,340
your name is holy and great.

780
00:52:25,900 --> 00:52:46,760
Father, we pray that your kingdom would come in our lives as it is in heaven, in our families as it is in heaven, in this church as it is in heaven, in our city as it is in heaven, across this great country as it is in heaven, so that you might get glory and honor and praise.

781
00:52:49,720 --> 00:52:58,140
God, I pray that you take whatever was shared this morning from the songs, to the conversations in the lobby, to this message, to our time in communion.

782
00:52:58,140 --> 00:53:02,360
You take all of it and you do with it what you want to do with it in the lives of individual believers.

783
00:53:02,360 --> 00:53:03,920
May we be submitted to your spirit.

784
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:08,480
May we take whatever we heard today back to you.

785
00:53:08,480 --> 00:53:16,560
God, may you be faithful to conform us into your image for your glory.

786
00:53:16,560 --> 00:53:18,060
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

787
00:53:18,060 --> 00:53:18,760
Amen.

788
00:53:18,760 --> 00:53:21,080
All right.

789
00:53:21,080 --> 00:53:21,960
We are going to.
